Why is object oriented better than procedural programming?
	Object-Oriented Programming is preferred over Procedural Programming because it organizes software into objects that combine data and behavior. This leads to better code organization, reusability, maintainability, scalability, and security. Features such as Encapsulation, Inheritance, Polymorphism, and Abstraction make OOP especially suitable for building large and complex applications, while procedural programming is generally more suitable for small, simple programs.
